     "chemical change",
     "physical change",
     "new substance"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "In a chemical change a new substance forms and it is usually not easily reversed. Burning wood, rusting iron, cooking food and curdling milk are chemical changes.\nIn a physical change the substance stays the same, as when ice melts.\nSigns of a chemical change are a new colour, gas, heat, light or a new smell."
    }
